= Common ground — Simple =

'''Common ground''' is information that people in a conversation treat as shared or mutually accepted.

If two people are standing outside in heavy rain, they do not need to explain every time that it is raining. That fact can be part of what they both treat as obvious in the conversation.

Common ground helps people use short references, understand [[Presupposition/Simple|presuppositions]], and follow what a conversation is about.

It is not the same as truth. People can share a mistaken belief.

It is also not all of [[Context (linguistics)/Simple|context]]. Context can include time, place, visible objects, and other information that may not be mutually accepted.

